# ~/.mcp/env/notion.env — Notion MCP reference (Keychain-backed, no file needed at runtime)
#
# The Notion MCP reads its token from macOS Keychain, not this file.
# This file documents the Keychain item and setup command only.
#
# Setup (run once per machine):
#   make secrets-notion
#
# Or manually:
#   security add-generic-password -s "claude-mcp-notion" -a "claude-code" -w "YOUR_TOKEN" login.keychain
#
# Keychain item:
#   service  (-s): claude-mcp-notion
#   account  (-a): claude-code
#
# Get your token at: https://www.notion.so/my-integrations
# New integration → give it a name → copy the "Internal Integration Token"
